From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:50:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] control: search and freeze the memory of the running
 app (cheats)

A memory cheat engine in the way of the Sorcerer tool on S60, behind the
control API:

- GET /v1/cheats: the app that has the focus, the search and the codes
- POST /v1/cheats/search {width, value?}: addresses holding the value,
  or a copy of the memory when the value is not known
- POST /v1/cheats/search/next {compare, value?}: keep the addresses equal
  to or different from a value, lower or higher than (or equal to) the
  value before, changed or unchanged
- GET /v1/cheats/search/results, POST /v1/cheats/codes,
  PATCH|DELETE /v1/cheats/codes/{index}: keep a result, write it, freeze it
- POST /v1/cheats/codes/restore: freeze again the codes saved frozen

Only the app's own chunks are read (heaps, stacks, static data), page by
page through its page table. The work runs on the emulator thread between
two CPU slices, through the new system::run_between_slices and
add_slice_callback, where no guest code runs and no system call is
served; frozen values are written again after every slice. Codes are
saved per app in cheats/<UID>.json and come back unfrozen.
